Practical Examination Write-Up: Experiment 11
1. AIM
To study physical transmission media (CAT6 Unshielded Twisted Pair) and fabricate network cables by demonstrating the crimping of RJ45 modular connectors according to TIA/EIA-568A and TIA/EIA-568B wiring standards for Straight-Through and Crossover cable configurations.

2. THEORY
Category 6 (CAT6) UTP Cable:
Contains 4 pairs of 24 AWG solid or stranded copper conductors enclosed in a PVC outer jacket.
Features internal longitudinal spline/separator to isolate pairs and minimize Near-End Crosstalk (NEXT) and Alien Crosstalk.
Supports bandwidth up to 250 MHz and 10BASE-T, 100BASE-TX, 1000BASE-T (Gigabit Ethernet) up to 100m, and 10GBASE-T up to 55m.
RJ45 Modular Connector: 8-Position, 8-Contact (8P8C) plug with gold-plated contact blades that pierce the wire insulation during crimping.
TIA/EIA Wiring Color Standards:
T568A Standard:
White-Green | 2. Green | 3. White-Orange | 4. Blue | 5. White-Blue | 6. Orange | 7. White-Brown | 8. Brown
T568B Standard (Industry Default):
White-Orange | 2. Orange | 3. White-Green | 4. Blue | 5. White-Blue | 6. Green | 7. White-Brown | 8. Brown
Cable Types & Application:
Straight-Through Cable: Both ends crimped with identical standards (T568B 
